// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5995 Add 4 detection rules for LLM and MCP attack surface
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5995
// Pull request author: ipunithgowda
// Change: new rule
// Title: Claude Code Session Token Or Bearer Header In Command Line - Linux
// Sigma ID: 1b9306f4-61af-4d4d-af4d-60229dd391c1
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Punith Gowda (Network Intelligence)
// Date: 2026-05-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552.001
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects credential leakage where a Claude or generic LLM bearer token appears in the visible
//   command line of a process. Looks for sk-ant-... session strings and 'Authorization: Bearer sk-'
//   style headers passed via curl, wget, or direct API invocation. Anything in argv is readable by
//   any local user via /proc and is preserved in shell history and audit logs.
// False positives:
//   - Internal red-team or pentest tooling that intentionally passes tokens via curl for replay testing
//   - Smoke-test scripts in CI that should be migrated to read from a secret manager rather than argv
// References:
//   - https://docs.anthropic.com/en/api/getting-started
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/
//   - https://owasp.org/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/
//   - https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/214.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/58c8781964014aba73b404e32ceafbb27d6668c8/rules-emerging-threats/2026/AI/proc_creation_lnx_claude_session_token_in_cmdline.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/curl" or FolderPath endswith "/wget" or FolderPath endswith "/http" or FolderPath endswith "/httpie") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "Authorization: Bearer sk-" or ProcessCommandLine contains "x-api-key: sk-ant-" or ProcessCommandLine contains "x-api-key:sk-ant-")
